class Solution {
    public int totalFruit(int[] fruits) {
        Map<Integer, Integer> mp = new HashMap<>();
        int max=Integer.MIN_VALUE, left=0;
        for(int i=0; i<fruits.length; i++){
            if(mp.containsKey(fruits[i])){
                mp.put(fruits[i], mp.get(fruits[i])+1);
            }else{
                mp.put(fruits[i],1);
            }
            while(mp.size()>2){
                mp.put(fruits[left],mp.get(fruits[left])-1);
                if(mp.get(fruits[left])==0){
                    mp.remove(fruits[left]);
                }
                left++;
            }
            max=Math.max(max,i-left+1);
        }
        return max;
    }
}

Time Complexity - O(N)
Space Complexity: O(1) — The map never stores more than $3$ keys before the while loop kicks in to remove the excess key.

Instead of counting how many times the while loop runs on one specific turn, count how many times each line can execute over the entire lifetime of the program:

Outer for loop:
Variable i goes from 0 to n - 1.
Executes exactly n times.

Inner while loop:
Every time the while loop runs, left increments by 1 (left++).

Since left starts at 0 and can never exceed n, the statement left++ can execute at most n times in total across all iterations combined.
Total Operations = Total outer steps + Total inner steps = n + n = 2n

Since constants are dropped in asymptotic analysis:O(2n) = O(n)
